From: WP2 Merged-Image Integrator <integrator@rg35xxh.local>
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] jive_framework: public-API event queue length
Upstream: squeezeplay@758bc11 src/squeezeplay/src/ui/jive_framework.c
Rationale: the perfwarn queue diagnostic called SDL_EventQueueLength(), an
 SDL-1.2 internal symbol that sdl12-compat (the runtime libSDL on target,
 same SONAME) intentionally does not export. With Ubuntu's default
 BIND_NOW, jive aborted at startup with "symbol lookup error" even though
 the call sits behind `if (perfwarn.queue)` (default 0, never taken in
 normal operation). SDL_PeepEvents(NULL, 0, SDL_PEEKEVENT, SDL_ALLEVENTS)
 is the documented public-API queue count and behaves identically on
 SDL 1.2.15 and sdl12-compat (same TU already uses SDL_PeepEvents).
Review: integrator-owned fix, needs Agent 2 (Core) review at merge;
 symbol-level sweep of the staged image shows this was the only
 non-libc/non-jive undefined symbol (see docs/test-results/wp2int-image.md).
 Behavior with perfwarn.queue enabled is unchanged (same count source).

diff --git a/src/squeezeplay/src/ui/jive_framework.c b/src/squeezeplay/src/ui/jive_framework.c
index 568c7db4..96f7d72c 100644
--- a/src/squeezeplay/src/ui/jive_framework.c
+++ b/src/squeezeplay/src/ui/jive_framework.c
@@ -457,10 +457,13 @@ static int jiveL_process_events(lua_State *L) {
 		jive_sdlevent_pump(L);
 	}

-	/* check queue size */
+	/* check queue size (public-API queue length: SDL_PeepEvents with
+	 * NULL/0 peeks the count; SDL_EventQueueLength() is an SDL-internal
+	 * symbol that sdl12-compat does not export) */
 	if (perfwarn.queue) {
-		if (SDL_EventQueueLength() > perfwarn.queue) {
-			printf("SDL_event_queue > %2d : %3d\n", perfwarn.queue, SDL_EventQueueLength());
+		int queue_len = SDL_PeepEvents(NULL, 0, SDL_PEEKEVENT, SDL_ALLEVENTS);
+		if (queue_len > perfwarn.queue) {
+			printf("SDL_event_queue > %2d : %3d\n", perfwarn.queue, queue_len);
 		}
 	}

